      "content": "* [CRITICAL] [LOGIC] Always-true role check grants manage access to all users (line: `if user.role == \"admin\" or \"owner\"`)\n  - Issue: `or \"owner\"` is a truthy string, so the condition evaluates as `(user.role == \"admin\") or True`, which is always True. Every logged-in user gets `can_manage = True` in their session, not just admins/owners.\n  - Fix: Change to `if user.role in (\"admin\", \"owner\"):` or `if user.role == \"admin\" or user.role == \"owner\":`.\n\n* [CRITICAL] [ERROR_HANDLING] `refresh_session` coroutine never awaited (line: `refresh_session(user.id)`)\n  - Issue: `refresh_session` is an `async def` function. Calling it without `await` creates a coroutine object that is immediately discarded. The session rotation (revoke old ID, issue new one) never executes, defeating the session fixation protection the function is meant to provide.\n  - Fix: Change to `await refresh_session(user.id)`.",
